IN THE SUPREME COURT OF INDIA
CASE NO: Civil Appeal No. 10842 of 2018
CITATION: (2023) 7 SCC 1
YEAR: 2023

CORAM / BENCH:
Hon'ble Judges: K.M. Joseph, Ajay Rastogi, Aniruddha Bose, Hrishikesh Roy, C.T. Ravikumar

PARTIES:
N.N. Global vs Indo Unique Flame

STATUTES & ACTS REFERRED:
Indian Stamp Act, 1899, Arbitration and Conciliation Act, 1996

KEY PROVISIONS & SECTIONS:
Section 35 Stamp Act, Section 11 Arbitration Act

LEGAL KEYWORDS & TOPICS:
unstamped contract, arbitration agreement validity, subsequently overruled

================================================================================
                    JUDGMENT SUMMARY & RATIO DECIDENDI
================================================================================

Historical ruling on unstamped arbitration clauses which held such agreements unenforceable, subsequently overruled by the unanimous 7-judge curative bench in December 2023.

1. ISSUES CONSIDERED:
   The court addressed questions of legal interpretation under Section 35 Stamp Act, Section 11 Arbitration Act.

2. ANALYSIS & PRECEDENT CONTEXT:
   Having examined the statutory scheme, fundamental principles of jurisprudence,
   and constitutional safeguards, the Court reiterated the necessity of strict
   compliance with statutory procedure and evidentiary standards.

3. HELD & BINDING RATIO:
   The principle formulated in this judgment constitutes binding judicial precedent
   within its territorial and appellate jurisdiction.

